- How does the solution change with unlimited cooldown or different cooldown durations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a non-trivial partition DP with a non-linear subarray cost and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions
- Range maximum queries (precomputation or on-the-fly)
- Path reconstruction via predecessor table

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  // precompute max for all ranges
  const mx = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++){ mx[i][i]=A[i]; for(let j=i+1;j<n;j++) mx[i][j]=Math.max(mx[i][j-1], A[j]); }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(Infinity));
  const prv = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1] = mx[0][i-1]*(i);
  for(let j=2;j<=k;j++){
    for(let i=j;i<=n;i++){
      for(let t=j-1;t<=i-1;t++){
        const cost = dp[t][j-1] + mx[t][i-1]*(i-t);
        if(cost < dp[i][j]){ dp[i][j]=cost; prv[i][j]=t; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {cost: dp[n][k], cutPoints: []};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- Can you optimize space to O(n) per k?
- How to handle equal costs and tie-breaking?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests counting paths with variable step lengths using DP, a common interview pattern in operations and logistics contexts.

## Key Concepts
- 1D DP for path counting
- Handling variable jump lengths
- Modulo arithmetic for large counts

## Code Example
```javascript
function countWays(jumps){
  const n = jumps.length;
  const MOD = 1000000007;
  const dp = new Array(n).fill(0);
  dp[0] = 1;
  for(let i = 0; i < n; i++){
    const maxJump = Math.min(jumps[i], n - 1 - i);
    for(let s = 1; s <= maxJump; s++){
      dp[i + s] = (dp[i + s] + dp[i]) % MOD;
    }
  }
  return dp[n - 1] || 0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you optimize to O(n) time if maxJump can be large but jumps form a sliding window of contributions?
- How would you adjust for different termination criteria or multiple destinations?

