## Why This Is Asked
Models practical scheduling under capacity with a convex (squared) day cost, exercising 2D DP and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes and days
- Transition constrained by daily capacity D
- Prefix sums for O(1) range sums
- Backtracking via parent pointers to recover daily blocks
- Complexity: O(n^2 m) time, O(n m) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostSchedule(A, m, D) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i - 1] + A[i - 1];
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(m + 1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(m + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let d = 1; d <= m; d++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
        const sum = pref[i] - pref[j];
        if (sum <= D && dp[j][d - 1] !== INF) {
          const cost = dp[j][d - 1] + sum * sum;
          if (cost < dp[i][d]) {
            dp[i][d] = cost;
            par[i][d] = j;
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  if (dp[n][m] === INF) return { cost: -1, blocks: [] };
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, d = m;
  while (d > 0) {
    const j = par[i][d];
    blocks.push([j + 1, i]);
    i = j;
    d--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return { cost: dp[n][m], blocks };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you optimize to near O(n m) if D is small or sums have tighter bounds?
- How would you present the actual day blocks to the user, including start/end indices and sums?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a novel fixed-gap non-crossing pairing constraint, a natural extension of classic non-crossing matching problems, while probing DP state design and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes with fixed pair distance
- Non-crossing/disjoint constraint handling
- Backpointers for reconstruction
- Space/time optimization trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxFixedGapPairs(A, d, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(false));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
      if (t > 0 && i - d - 1 >= 0) {
        const cand = dp[i - d - 1][t - 1] + A[i - 1] * A[i - d - 1];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = cand;
          take[i][t] = true;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  const pairs = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    if (take[i][t]) {
      pairs.push([i - d, i]); // 1-based indices of the pair
      i = i - d - 1;
      t--;
    } else {
      i--;
    }
  }
  pairs.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], pairs };
}
```
